    {
      "title": "Large Language Models (LLMs) have accelerated the deep\nlearning revolution, driving upheaval in healthcare, defense,\nfinance, education, etc. The computational demands of early\nneural networks ushered in specialized accelerators, but the\nmassive compute needs of LLMs has pushed deployment to\nthe cloud, atop acceleration. While this transition to cloud-\nbacked inference serving enables remarkable capabilities, it\nalso forces customers (enterprises and individuals) to surrender\nownership and control of their data to the ethereal cloud. This\nsurrender of data ownership is a pressing issue due to its\nsocietal implications, including mass exposure of citizens' data",
      "heading_level": null,
